  "style": {
    "id": "tensegrity",
    "name": "Tensegrity",
    "description": "A tensegrity tower on a bright studio table: three levels of pale wooden struts, each pair of strut ends joined only by taut red cords, so no strut touches another. The shape is SOLVED, not keyframed (tower.js): a static balance of nearly rigid struts and tension-only elastic cords gives the standing shape under prestress, the shape with a brass weight on the top three nodes, and the slumped shape after one cord is cut, where strut-on-strut contact is what finally holds it. Every cord's tension sets its glow and the pitch of its pluck; the slump runs along the solver's own damped descent between the two solved poses on an art-directed clock.",
